    sales: 'Farmers, food companies and regulators pay. They trust field results and local references. First skill: a simple service menu and one named reference.',
    watch: 'Choosing it as a fallback, then meeting seasons, travel and field reality unprepared.',
  },
  {
    badge: 'Lane 6',
    title: 'Research in physical and life sciences',
    tone: 'violet',
    scale: 'low',
    why: 'A long ladder with competition at several stages, and few reach stable senior posts. Keep a data or writing skill running that can grow on its own.',
    entry: 'BSc, or IISER BS-MS through the IISER Aptitude Test, then MSc, NET or GATE-type routes and a PhD.',
    ai: 'Leverage is high: literature review, analysis, coding. Pressure falls on routine analysis, so the question you ask and the way you check results are the human edge.',
    sales: 'Mostly employer-only: universities, institutes and company research teams. The sales layer matters for the move around it, such as data consulting, science writing or training.',
    watch: 'A postgraduate degree taken only to delay a decision.',
  },
  {
    badge: 'Lane 7',
    title: 'Medicine and dentistry',
    tone: 'gold',
    scale: 'low',
    why: 'Very few seats, a seat to win at undergraduate level and again at postgraduate level, and many years before pay grows.',
